h largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex in degeneracy order, among that vertex’s later neighbors, so memory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stays O(n + m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. Exponential in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worst case."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficients()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clusteringCoefficients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques22ClusteringCoefficientsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of the simple graph (self-loops ignored,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges counted once), in one compact-forward pass. O(m^(3\/2))."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficients()","role":"symbol","title":"clusteringCoefficients()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount(of:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"triangleCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{